This happens for `correct-fs-dirs`.
This is kinda major. Perfectly valid inputs sometimes get misclassified by the mm
`url-scheme` dispatcher fn due to an incorrect/incomplete implementation.

```
(correct-fs-dirs)
=>
(#object [java.io.File 0x5163fef3 "/Users/me"] ; <~ false
 #object [sun.nio.fs.UnixPath 0x1f2bf9ef "/Users/me"] ; <~ false
 #object [java.net.URL 0x66c9be6a "file:/Users/me/"]
 #object [java.net.URI 0x6beb06f2 "file:///Users/me/"]
 "/Users/me" ; <~ false
 "file:/Users/me"
 "/Users/me/" ; <~ false
 "file:/Users/me/"
 #object [java.io.File 0x5b8a6621 "/Users/me/Desktop/Projects/OSS/resauce/test/resauce"] ; <~ false
 #object [sun.nio.fs.UnixPath 0x95233fe "/Users/me/Desktop/Projects/OSS/resauce/test/resauce"] ; <~ false
 #object [java.net.URL 0x5574e811 "file:/Users/me/Desktop/Projects/OSS/resauce/test/resauce/"]
 #object [java.net.URI 0x4c41e8e3 "file:///Users/me/Desktop/Projects/OSS/resauce/test/resauce/"]
 "/Users/me/Desktop/Projects/OSS/resauce/test/resauce" ; <~ false
